# bakepreprocess

- Label: Bake Pre-Process
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 2
- Parameters: 24 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/bakepreprocess.html
- Summary (EN): Prepares a low-resolution mesh for texture baking by generating a cage, ray directions and ray lengths, and provides an interactive viewport state to preview the rays and cage positions. The page states that this COP is a direct copy of the Bake Pre-Process SOP, and that a Bake Setup recipe creates it automatically. Available since Houdini 22.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Prépare un maillage basse résolution au bake en générant la cage, les directions et les longueurs de rayons, avec un aperçu interactif.

- Inputs meaning: ["low: low-resolution geometry used to build the cage", "high: high-resolution geometry, passed through unchanged for comparison with the cage"]

- Key parameters: ["Normal Mode: keep geometric normals, smooth them into point normals, or override them", "Missing Normals: from messages and warnings to errors, or silent creation", "Ray Start Offset and Ray Start Mode: cage extent, uniform or scaled by an attribute", "Ray Direction: toward the matching low-res polygons, or from a float3 vertex attribute", "Ray End Offset and Ray End Mode: sets ray length; No End writes -1 for endless rays", "Soften Cage and Soften Mode: split by faces, UV seams or an edge group", "Cage outputs: Ray Start (point), Ray Direction (vertex), Ray Length (point)"]

- Caveats: ["Baking works best when the low-res mesh has normals; without them the node may warn or error", "From Low Vertex Attribute requires a float3 vertex attribute on the low-res mesh", "By UV Seams requires a UV attribute", "Ray length is the difference between the end and start offsets", "The page states the COP and the SOP can produce the same result"]

